---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Home — Editorial
theme: editorial
permalink: /explore/editorial/
description: Recruiting and staffing for students starting out and professionals moving on — plus the employers who hire both.
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   EDITORIAL — a magazine feature, not a stack of marketing blocks.
   One masthead opener, then a single running article column with a
   sticky "in this issue" sidebar of facts alongside it — the sidebar
   carries the stats/employers/services data points a brochure would
   normally give their own full-width sections to. Nothing after the
   masthead is a discrete full-bleed block until the closing CTA.
   ================================================================ #}

{# ---------- 1. Masthead: type, then a wide photo with a mono caption ---------- #}
<section class="section-container pt-12 pb-14 sm:pt-20">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-x-6 gap-y-10">
    <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-3 lg:pt-4">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45">Est. 2013 — Chicago, IL</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-[24ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">
        A recruiting practice for people at the start of a career and people in the middle of one.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center -space-x-2.5">
        {% for face in ["priya", "sofia", "james", "aisha", "daniel"] %}
        <img src="{{ ('/assets/images/home/person-' + face + '.jpg') | url }}" alt="" width="36" height="36" loading="eager"
             class="photo-warm h-9 w-9 rounded-full object-cover ring-2 ring-paper">
        {% endfor %}
        <span class="!ml-4 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink/50">Recently placed</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-9">
      <h1 class="font-display text-[3.25rem] font-semibold leading-[0.92] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[5.5rem] lg:text-[7.25rem]">
        Where careers<br>
        find their <em class="not-italic text-accent">footing</em>.
      </h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figure class="mt-12">
    <div class="photo-frame aspect-[16/7] w-full">
      <img src="{{ '/assets/images/home/hero-team-meeting.jpg' | url }}" alt="A recruiter and two candidates talking around a table"
           width="1400" height="613" fetchpriority="high"
           class="photo-warm h-full w-full object-cover">
    </div>
    <figcaption class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-1 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink/45 sm:flex-row sm:justify-between">
      <span>Fig. 01 — Placement review, Wabash Ave office</span>
      <span>Every match is made by a person who read the résumé</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-12 gap-x-6 gap-y-8 border-t border-ink pt-8">
    <p class="col-span-12 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75 md:col-span-6 lg:col-span-5">
      We match people to work worth doing, and employers to talent worth hiring — one conversation at a time, never by keyword filter.
    </p>
    <div class="col-span-12 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row md:col-span-6 md:justify-end lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9">
      <a href="{{ '/services/job-placement/' | url }}" class="btn-primary">Find a Job</a>
      <a href="{{ '/services/recruitment-staffing/' | url }}" class="btn-outline">Hire Talent</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 2. The feature: one article column + a running sidebar ---------- #}
<section class="section-container border-t border-ink/15 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-x-10">

    {# -- Article column -- #}
    <article class="lg:col-span-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45">§ 01 — Position</p>
      <blockquote class="mt-4">
        <p class="font-display text-2xl leading-[1.24] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Most agencies optimise for volume. We optimise for the
          <span class="border-b-4 border-accent">second year</span> —
          whether the person is still in the role, still growing, still glad they took the call.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 border-t border-ink/15 pt-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">For job seekers</p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">You've sent the applications. Send one conversation instead — profile rebuilt around the work you want, introductions to verified employers, prep before every interview, negotiation help on the offer.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">For employers</p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Fewer résumés, better ones. A brief taken by the person who owns it, shortlists instead of dumps, background checks in-house, time-to-fill under four weeks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-10 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45 border-t border-ink/15 pt-8">§ 02 — Case study</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink sm:text-[2.4rem]">
        Forty applications, no replies. Then two weeks.
      </h2>
      <figure class="photo-frame mt-6 aspect-[16/9]">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/images/home/interview-conversation.jpg' | url }}" alt="A candidate in conversation with a hiring manager"
             width="1400" height="788" loading="lazy" class="photo-warm h-full w-full object-cover">
      </figure>
      <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
        Priya had a strong analytics background and a résumé that buried it on page two. We rebuilt the profile around the work she actually wanted, introduced her to three employers who needed exactly that, and prepped her for each conversation.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="mt-6 border-l-4 border-accent pl-5 font-display text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink">
        &ldquo;The role fit better than anything I'd found on my own.&rdquo;
        <footer class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink/50">Priya Nandakumar, Data Analyst — Amazon</footer>
      </blockquote>

      <p class="mt-10 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45 border-t border-ink/15 pt-8">§ 03 — Sectors</p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
        Share of placements over the last twelve months. We say no to sectors we don't know — a recruiter who claims all of them knows none of them.
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-5 divide-y divide-ink/10 border-y border-ink/15">
        {% for industry in industries.list %}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 py-3">
          <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ industry.name }} <span class="font-normal text-ink/50">— {{ industry.roles }}</span></dt>
          <dd class="shrink-0 font-mono text-sm text-ink/60">{{ industry.share }}</dd>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </dl>

      <p class="mt-10 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">No experience yet?</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-[1.14] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink sm:text-3xl">
        Most training providers hand you a certificate. <span class="border-b-4 border-accent">We hand you the interview.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
        Our IT Training tracks end where every other course stops — graduates go straight into the same placement pipeline as everyone else in this piece. Same recruiters, same employers, no separate queue.
      </p>
      <a href="{{ '/services/it-training/' | url }}" class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b-2 border-accent pb-0.5 font-medium text-ink transition-all hover:gap-3">
        See the training tracks {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
      </a>

      <figure class="mt-12 border-y border-ink py-10">
        <p class="font-display text-2xl leading-[1.3] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          &ldquo;I was switching fields at thirty-four and every recruiter treated that as a problem to explain away. These ones treated it as the story.&rdquo;
        </p>
        <figcaption class="mt-5 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink/50">
          Lena Toma — DevOps Engineer, Nvidia
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="mt-10 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45">§ 04 — Process</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink sm:text-3xl">How it actually goes.</h2>
      <ol class="mt-5 divide-y divide-ink/15 border-t border-ink">
        {% set edSteps = [
          { label: "Apply", description: "Tell us where you are and where you want to be — takes ten minutes." },
          { label: "Match", description: "We connect you with roles and employers that actually fit the brief." },
          { label: "Interview", description: "Coaching and prep before every conversation that matters." },
          { label: "Placement", description: "An offer, a negotiation assist, and a check-in 90 days in." }
        ] %}
        {% for step in edSteps %}
        <li class="flex items-baseline gap-5 py-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">{{ step.label }}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/65">{{ step.description }}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-10 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45 border-t border-ink/15 pt-8">§ 05 — Voices</p>
      <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-6 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {% set featuredElsewhere = ["priya", "lena"] %}
        {% for testimonial in testimonials.list %}
        {% if testimonial.slug not in featuredElsewhere and loop.index <= 4 %}
        <figure class="border-t border-ink pt-5">
          <blockquote class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/75">&ldquo;{{ testimonial.quote }}&rdquo;</blockquote>
          <figcaption class="mt-4 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink/50">{{ testimonial.name }} — {{ testimonial.role }}, {{ testimonial.company }}</figcaption>
        </figure>
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </article>

    {# -- Sidebar: the numbers a brochure would give full sections to -- #}
    <aside class="mt-14 lg:col-span-4 lg:mt-0">
      <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 space-y-8 border-t border-ink pt-6 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:border-ink/15 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0">

        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45">By the numbers</p>
          <dl class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-y-5">
            {% for stat in stats.list %}
            <div>
              <dd class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight text-ink"
                  data-count-up data-target="{{ stat.value }}" data-suffix="{{ stat.suffix }}">0{{ stat.suffix }}</dd>
              <dt class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink/50">{{ stat.label }}</dt>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
          </dl>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-ink/15 pt-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45">Services in this piece</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 divide-y divide-ink/10">
            {% for service in services.list %}
            <li>
              <a href="{{ service.url | url }}" class="group flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-2.5 text-sm text-ink transition-colors hover:text-accent">
                {{ service.title }}
                <span class="text-ink/30 transition-all group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:text-accent">{{ icon("arrow-right", "w-3.5 h-3.5") }}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-ink/15 pt-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45">Referenced employers</p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink/60 text-sm">
            {% for company in companies.list %}{{ company.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-t border-ink/15 pt-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink/45">What we won't budge on</p>
          <ol class="mt-3 space-y-4">
            {% set beliefs = [
              { n: "01", t: "Careers, not jobs" },
              { n: "02", t: "A person reads it" },
              { n: "03", t: "Deadlines are deadlines" },
              { n: "04", t: "The relationship outlasts the placement" }
            ] %}
            {% for belief in beliefs %}
            <li class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">{{ belief.n }}</span>
              <span class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{{ belief.t }}</span>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 3. Live placement feed (the one other full-bleed interlude) ---------- #}
{% include "partials/placement-feed.njk" %}

{# ---------- 4. CTA ---------- #}
<section class="bg-ink py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="section-container text-center">
    <h2 class="mx-auto max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] text-paper sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">
      Ready to find your footing?
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-paper/60">
      Whether you're job hunting or hiring, the first conversation is free.
    </p>
    <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}" class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center gap-3 border-b-2 border-accent pb-1 font-display text-2xl text-paper transition-all hover:gap-5 sm:text-3xl">
      Start the conversation {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-6 h-6") }}
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "partials/variant-switcher.njk" %}
